+1. A red test per ID first (unit tests in test/fix-viz-5.test.js, e2e in test/e2e/fix-viz-5.e2e.js registered in scripts/e2e.js), failing before and passing after; the reviewers' red tests for your IDs must pass after your fix (say which ones already pass on fbdad58: pay-at-place fixed V-35 to V-40).
+2. Phones: every visible change checked at every size in test/e2e/phone-sizes.mjs (PHONES and POSTURES: 280x653 to 1114x720, the Razr cover 352x355 and the landscapes). Run `node test/e2e/webkit/phone-smoke.mjs --dist dist --sizes all --engines chromium` and test/e2e/phone-matrix.e2e.js before and after: no regressions. Use real touch (CDP `Input.dispatchTouchEvent`) for taps (PLAYBOOK, Known traps).
+3. Light and dark, and the colour-blind views the reviewer used; contrast at the floors in docs/process/viz-review-beta-2.md §5.
+4. Screenshots before and after for each visible change, phone and desktop, light and dark, in docs/screenshots/fix-viz-5/, shrunk with `bash scripts/cycle/shrink-screenshots.sh docs/screenshots/fix-viz-5`.
+5. Don't regress: viz-even's tests (test/viz-even.test.js, test/e2e/viz-even.e2e.js), fix-pay-at-place's (`payAt` is the one rule for pay at a place; use it, never the headline, for a place), fix-touch-tips' tooltip behaviour (sticky tips on phones), the keyboard and aria of the chart (aria-activedescendant, roles), and the chart's draw time.
